{
  "html": [
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Example Topic is a subject of study first described in the nineteenth century. It has been the focus of sustained academic attention ever since, and the literature covering it now spans several disciplines and many hundreds of published papers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "h2",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Background"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Early accounts of the topic were largely anecdotal, drawing on field notes and correspondence between a small number of researchers working in different countries without a shared vocabulary for what they were observing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "A more systematic approach emerged once instrumentation improved. Measurements that had previously taken weeks could be repeated in an afternoon, and the resulting datasets made it possible to compare observations across sites for the first time."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "h2",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Methods"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
