          "attributes": [
            [
              "alt",
              "Field site"
            ],
            [
              "src",
              "https://encyclopedia.example.com/images/field-site.jpg"
            ]
          ],
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "A typical "
        },
        {
          "kind": "element",
          "name": "a",
          "attributes": [
            [
              "href",
              "https://encyclopedia.example.com/wiki/Field_site"
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "field site"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Instruments and sites"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Contemporary studies rely on a standard protocol agreed at a working conference. Samples are collected on a fixed schedule, catalogued at the point of collection, and cross-checked by a second team before any analysis begins."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Critics have argued that the protocol privileges reproducibility over sensitivity, and that unusual cases are discarded before anyone has a chance to examine them closely. Defenders reply that the tradeoff is what makes comparison across sites possible at all."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "h2",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Results"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "The consolidated dataset shows a consistent seasonal pattern that had been suspected but never demonstrated across more than one site at a time. The effect is strongest in the spring and weakest in late autumn."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Secondary analyses have identified a smaller regional variation layered on top of the seasonal pattern. Whether this reflects genuine local differences or artifacts of instrumentation remains unsettled."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "h2",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Reception"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Reviews of the consolidated dataset have been broadly positive, though several commentators have noted that the sampling schedule was designed around institutional convenience rather than the underlying phenomenon."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "h2",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Legacy"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "The protocol has since been adopted by adjacent fields, and the vocabulary it introduced is now standard in textbooks. Later work has largely extended rather than overturned the original findings."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
